 The matrix
\[\begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{pmatrix}\]is not invertible if and only if its determinant is 0.  We calculate the determinant as follows:
\begin{align*}
\det \begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{pmatrix} &= a \begin{vmatrix} c & a \\ a & b \end{vmatrix} - b \begin{vmatrix} b & a \\ c & b \end{vmatrix} + c \begin{vmatrix} b & c \\ c & a \end{vmatrix} \\
&= a(bc - a^2) - b(b^2 - ac) + c(ab - c^2) \\
&= 3abc - (a^3 + b^3 + c^3).
\end{align*}By the factorization $x^3 + y^3 + z^3 - 3xyz = (x + y + z)(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - xy - xz - yz),$ we have that $x^3 + y^3 + z^3 = 3xyz$ if and only if $x + y + z = 0$ or $x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - xy - xz - yz = 0.$

If $x + y + z = 0,$ then
\begin{align*}
\frac{a}{b + c} + \frac{b}{a cyclic sums(b + c)c} &= 3 - \frac{a^2 + b^2 + c^2}{ab + ac + bc} \\
&= 3 - \frac{(a + b + c)^2 - 2ab - ac - bc}{ab + ac + bc} \\
&= 3 - \frac{(a + b + c)^2}{ab + ac + bc} + 2 \\
&= 5 - \frac{(a + b + c)^2}{ab + ac + bc}.
\end{align*}Therefore, the only possible value of
\[\frac{a}{b + c} + \frac{b}{a + c} + \frac{c}{a + b}\]such that the matrix is not invertible is $\boxed{5}.$

